after:
Follow the count down to zero.

```csharp
int turns = 3;
while (turns > 0) {
    System.Console.WriteLine(turns);
    turns = turns - 1;
}
System.Console.WriteLine("Done");
```

It prints 3, 2, 1, and Done on separate lines. Zero is not greater than zero, so it is not printed inside the loop.
